{"tool_name":"long-read-tools","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"long-read-tools","home":"https://long-read-tools.org/","license":"MIT","summary":"Long-read-tools is an interactive database of software tools for the analysis of long read sequencing data.","addition_date":"2020-10-23T03:34:27Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:31:10.317443Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:long-read-tools","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"amarasinghe.s@wehi.edu.au","name":"Shanika L. Amarasinghe","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-2229-8106"},{"email":"gouil.q@wehi.edu.au","name":"Quentin Gouil","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-5142-7886"},{"email":"mritchie@wehi.edu.au","name":"Matthew E.\u00a0Ritchie","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-7383-0609","url":"https://www.wehi.edu.au/people/matthew-ritchie"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"note":"search tools for long-read sequencing analysis","operation":[{"term":"Operation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0004"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"long-read-tools","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"quentin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-020-1935-5","metadata":{"abstract":"Long-read technologies are overcoming early limitations in accuracy and throughput, broadening their application domains in genomics. Dedicated analysis tools that take into account the characteristics of long-read data are thus required, but the fast pace of development of such tools can be overwhelming. To assist in the design and analysis of long-read sequencing projects, we review the current landscape of available tools and present an online interactive database, long-read-tools.org, to facilitate their browsing. We further focus on the principles of error correction, base modification detection, and long-read transcriptomics analysis and highlight the challenges that remain.","authors":[{